## Architecture Decisions (Confirmed)

- **Frontend:** Next.js 14 App Router (already set up at `apps/web/`)
- **Backend:** Express API (already set up at `apps/api/`) — auth, notes, admin routes already exist
- **Database:** PostgreSQL via Prisma (schema already migrated, models ready)
- **Notes Storage:** **AWS S3** (same `@aws-sdk/client-s3` SDK — just change endpoint config in `.env`)
- **Secure Viewer:** PDF.js rendered on `<canvas>` — never exposes the raw file URL to the browser
- **Auth:** **Google Sign-In only** (Google Identity Services → ID token → `POST /api/auth/google`)
- **Mobile-first:** All pages designed for mobile first, then scaled up to desktop

### 3-Role System

| Role | Access |
|---|---|
| `SUPER_ADMIN` | Everything — users, content, other admin accounts |
| `CONTENT_MANAGER` | Upload/edit notes, manage announcements & subjects — no user management |
| `STUDENT` | View notes (all, since MVP has no gating), view homepage |

